<title>UK: BTL expands in Germany buying Ballauf Air.</title>
<headline>BTL expands in Germany buying Ballauf Air.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Wilson Group, the air and seafreight division of the BTL Group, said it has acquired Ballauf Air, an airfreight company specialising in international logistics packages.</p>
<p>Ballauf Air was formed in 1988 and is headquartered in Hamburg with a staff of almost 30 located at other key airports across Germany. Its primary customers operate in the garment, machinery and ship spares sectors.</p>
<p>&quot;The purchase of Ballauf Air is part of our globalisation process, and will give us a strong base in Germany on which to expand,&quot; said Wilson Group managing director Henrik von Sydow.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
